This file describes the repository as a whole. Nothing is published from the
repository root: each published package carries its own LICENSE and NOTICE,
and those per-package files are the authoritative notices for what ships in
that package's tarball:

  packages/core/NOTICE       unity-asset-reader
  packages/texture/NOTICE    unity-asset-reader-texture
  packages/node/NOTICE       unity-asset-reader-node
  packages/decoder/LICENSE   texture2ddecoder-wasm

They say which package uses which upstream, and for what. Runtime npm
dependencies are not inlined into any package's dist/ (plan section 2, #71),
so they ship with their own LICENSE files and are not listed here.

The reader packages are a derivative work: their Unity format handling is
hand-ported from the projects below. Their copyright notices are kept per
their licenses, and every ported source file carries a one-line attribution
to the file it was ported from.

